    "result_text": "The build is green. The full suite (the acceptance tests, which are the only test class present) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI derived `locality` from the owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table, following the codebase's existing patterns for derived, non-persisted fields (`membershipTier`, `initials`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`util/CityLocality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility utility mirroring `AddressNormalizer`. It holds the fixed table (`Sydney->NSW, Melbourne->VIC, Brisbane->QLD`) and `forCity(city)` returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for anything not in the table (including null).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived `getLocality()` getter that delegates to `CityLocality.forCity(city)`, matching how `getMembershipTier()` exposes derived state. MapStruct auto-maps it onto the DTO by name.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field into the JSON response.\n\nThe table logic lives in one focused util, the model just exposes it, and the mapper/DTO wiring is reused rather than duplicated. Both acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass.",
